// The raw-OKLCH gate for TypeScript and TSX. A numeric `oklch(` (one whose
// first channel is a number, not `from …`) in a string literal, a JSX
// attribute string or a template-literal chunk fails `biome ci`: colors come
// from the tokens in src/styles/tokens.css, as a utility (`bg-surface-1`), a
// `/N` modifier (`bg-plasma/15`), `var(--color-…)` or relative color syntax
// (`oklch(from var(--color-plasma) l c h / 0.15)`).
//
// biome.json scopes it: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}, without the colocated tests (they
// assert rendered values) and without the canvas, xterm, WebGPU and syntax
// highlighter consumers, which need concrete colors (useTerminal.ts,
// chart-theme.ts, particles.ts, postprocess.ts, syntax-highlight.ts).
//
// Known exceptions are keyed on file path plus literal value, not line, so
// moving code never breaks them: the literals the stage-1 token sweep left
// because no token matches them. A new value, or a known value in a new file,
// fails. Delete a line when its literal becomes a token; the Q-9 design
// direction names the rest. biome-plugins/no-raw-oklch-css.grit is the CSS
// twin; `pnpm check:raw-oklch` proves both still fail a raw literal.
language js

predicate known_raw_oklch($color) {
